# Mermaid diagrams (ARMIC)

All Mermaid in this repo must render readably on **GitHub** (light + dark UI). Canonical examples: `README.md`, `docs/architecture.md`, `docs/overview.md`.

## Required

1. **Explicit text color** on every styled node: `color:#ffffff` on dark fills (never rely on theme-default text).
2. **`classDef` + `class`** — do not use bare `style node fill:#e3f2fd` pastel fills.
3. **Flat graphs** — avoid empty subgraph wrappers (`subgraph ROW[" "]`) that add gray columns and wash out labels.
4. **Details in markdown** — keep edge labels short; put long copy in tables or prose below the diagram.
5. **End every styled diagram** with the shared palette block (pick roles that fit).

## Forbidden

- Pastel / light-only fills without dark text (`#e3f2fd`, `#fff3cd`, `#f3e5f5`, `#ffcdd2`, …)
- White or near-white node fills on GitHub (unreadable in dark mode)
- Emoji-only nodes with no text
- `%%{init: …}` theme overrides (GitHub support is inconsistent)

## ARMIC palette (copy as needed)

```mermaid
classDef step fill:#1e40af,color:#ffffff,stroke:#93c5fd,stroke-width:2px
classDef record fill:#5b21b6,color:#ffffff,stroke:#c4b5fd,stroke-width:2px
classDef mcu fill:#047857,color:#ffffff,stroke:#6ee7b7,stroke-width:2px
classDef io fill:#334155,color:#ffffff,stroke:#94a3b8,stroke-width:2px
classDef power fill:#b45309,color:#ffffff,stroke:#fcd34d,stroke-width:2px
classDef layer fill:#1e293b,color:#ffffff,stroke:#64748b,stroke-width:2px
classDef estop fill:#991b1b,color:#ffffff,stroke:#fca5a5,stroke-width:2px
```

| Role | classDef | Use for |
|------|----------|---------|
| Primary flow | `step` | Session steps, deploy steps, agent loop |
| Outcome / reward | `record` | Records, rewards, catalog endpoints |
| MCU / done | `mcu` | STM32 path, success terminus |
| I/O / hardware | `io` | PCA9685, arm, browser, wearable |
| Power rail | `power` | 12 V → buck → 5 V |
| Safety layers | `layer` | dry_run, watchdog, limits |
| E-STOP | `estop` | Final halt / home |

## Template — linear flow (session loop)

```mermaid
flowchart TD
    A["Step one"]
    B["Step two"]
    C["Outcome"]

    A --> B --> C --> A

    classDef step fill:#1e40af,color:#ffffff,stroke:#93c5fd,stroke-width:2px
    classDef record fill:#5b21b6,color:#ffffff,stroke:#c4b5fd,stroke-width:2px
    class A,B step
    class C record
```

Wrap the block above in a ` ```mermaid ` fence when embedding in markdown files.

## Template — dual brain (UNO Q)

Use **separate nodes**, not a nested subgraph box. MPU = `step`, MCU = `mcu`, peripherals = `io`.

## Before merging doc changes

- [ ] Every node in a styled diagram is assigned a `classDef`
- [ ] No pastel `style` lines remain
- [ ] Preview on GitHub (or assume dark mode) — text readable on every box
